    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of a square with a given perimeter, we first need to determine the length of one side of the square. \n\nThe formula for the perimeter (P) of a square is:\n\\[ P = 4s \\]\nwhere \\( s \\) is the length of one side of the square.\n\nGiven that the perimeter is 32 feet, we can set up the equation:\n\\[ 4s = 32 \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( s \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 4:\n\\[ s = \\frac{32}{4} \\]\n\\[ s = 8 \\]\n\nNow that we know the length of one side of the square is 8 feet, we can find the area (A) of the square using the formula:\n\\[ A = s^2 \\]\n\nSubstituting the value of \\( s \\) into the formula, we get:\n\\[ A = 8^2 \\]\n\\[ A = 64 \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{64}\\) square feet.",
