      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the area of a square, we need to first determine the length of one side of the square. The perimeter of a square is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Perimeter} = 4 \\times \\text{side length} \\]\n\nGiven that the perimeter is 32 feet, we can set up the equation:\n\n\\[ 32 = 4 \\times \\text{side length} \\]\n\nTo find the side length, we divide both sides of the equation by 4:\n\n\\[ \\text{side length} = \\frac{32}{4} = 8 \\text{ feet} \\]\n\nNow that we know the side length of the square is 8 feet, we can calculate the area of the square. The area of a square is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\text{side length}^2 \\]\n\nSubstituting the side length we found:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = 8^2 = 64 \\text{ square feet} \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{64} \\]",
